WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.867 --> 00:00:13.455
The next morning, Heidi opened her eyes.

2
00:00:13.456 --> 00:00:17.523
She was in a high bed facing two windows covered by long curtains.

3
00:00:17.524 --> 00:00:23.837
It was very different from her bed in the hayloft, with its view down the valley through the hole by her bed.

4
00:00:23.838 --> 00:00:26.698
Heidi jumped out of bed and ran to a window.

5
00:00:26.699 --> 00:00:31.108
The curtains were too heavy for her to push aside, so she crawled under them.

6
00:00:31.109 --> 00:00:33.966
Behind the curtains, the window was too high.

7
00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:37.485
She could only just peer out and couldn't find a way to open it.

8
00:00:37.486 --> 00:00:39.930
Suddenly there was a knock on her door.

9
00:00:39.931 --> 00:00:42.650
"Breakfast is ready," said the maid.

10
00:00:42.651 --> 00:00:46.652
Heidi had no idea what she was expected to do, so she waited.

11
00:00:46.653 --> 00:00:48.986
Shortly after, Fraulein appeared.

12
00:00:48.987 --> 00:00:52.915
"What is the matter with you, Heidi?" she said angrily.

13
00:00:52.916 --> 00:00:55.806
"Don't you understand what breakfast is?

14
00:00:55.807 --> 00:00:57.929
Come along at once!"

15
00:00:57.930 --> 00:01:00.612
Heidi had no difficulty understanding that.

16
00:01:00.613 --> 00:01:03.003
She followed Fraulein downstairs.

17
00:01:03.004 --> 00:01:06.882
The windows in the dining room were also too high for her to see out of.

18
00:01:06.883 --> 00:01:10.143
Heidi was starting to feel like she was in a prison.

19
00:01:10.144 --> 00:01:14.345
Clara had been at the breakfast table for a while and was smiling cheerfully.

20
00:01:14.346 --> 00:01:18.046
Heidi didn't know it, but Clara was often lonely and glum.

21
00:01:18.047 --> 00:01:24.581
Now that Heidi was staying with her, Clara was looking forward to all sorts of new fun.

22
00:01:24.582 --> 00:01:27.754
As soon as the children were alone, Heidi asked,

23
00:01:27.755 --> 00:01:30.802
"How can I open a window in my bedroom?"

24
00:01:30.803 --> 00:01:32.540
"You can ask Sebastian.

25
00:01:32.541 --> 00:01:35.974
He'll be happy to open one for you," Clara assured her.

26
00:01:35.975 --> 00:01:38.158
Heidi was very relieved.

27
00:01:38.159 --> 00:01:41.579
While the girls were eating breakfast, Clara's tutor arrived.

28
00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:45.344
Fraulein took him aside and told him all her worries about Heidi.

29
00:01:45.345 --> 00:01:50.442
He was a patient man and said that regular teaching would soon help her catch up to Clara.

30
00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:55.293
After breakfast, the girls joined him in the study and started their lesson.

31
00:01:55.294 --> 00:02:00.692
A little while later, Fraulein was walking past the study door when she heard a huge crash.

32
00:02:00.693 --> 00:02:03.049
"Look at the state of things!"

33
00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:05.569
exclaimed Fraulein when she opened the door.

34
00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:10.582
"Tablecloth, books, work basket, everything covered in ink.

35
00:02:10.583 --> 00:02:14.840
It was Heidi's fault, I suppose!"

36
00:02:14.841 --> 00:02:18.609
"Yes, but it was all an accident," said Clara.

37
00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:22.734
"Heidi heard the carriages passing outside, and they startled her."

38
00:02:22.735 --> 00:02:26.051
Fraulein was angry, but did not punish Heidi.

39
00:02:26.052 --> 00:02:33.309
Later that afternoon, while Clara took her nap, Heidi asked Sebastian where she could go to see out over the whole city.

40
00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:38.069
"You would have to climb to the top of a church tower," said Sebastian.

41
00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:42.631
With that in mind, Heidi set off in search of the highest tower she could find.

42
00:02:42.632 --> 00:02:46.317
On a street corner, she saw a boy with a hand organ and asked,

43
00:02:46.318 --> 00:02:49.656
"Do you know any churches with high towers?"

44
00:02:49.657 --> 00:02:51.514
"Yes, I know one.

45
00:02:51.515 --> 00:02:55.224
For two pennies, I will show you," the boy said.

46
00:02:55.225 --> 00:02:56.653
"Clara will pay you.

47
00:02:56.654 --> 00:02:58.979
She has money," Heidi agreed.

48
00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:02.467
"And will you help me find my way back home?" she asked.

49
00:03:02.468 --> 00:03:04.919
"Yes, for another two pennies."

50
00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:07.407
"Okay," said Heidi.

51
00:03:07.408 --> 00:03:10.251
The boy led her through the streets to an old church.

52
00:03:10.252 --> 00:03:15.889
A priest answered the bell and, holding her hand, led Heidi up the winding stairs.

53
00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:19.470
At the top, Heidi was disappointed.

54
00:03:19.471 --> 00:03:21.970
"I wanted to see the mountains.

55
00:03:21.971 --> 00:03:27.457
All I can see are roofs and towers and chimney tops!" she said.

56
00:03:27.458 --> 00:03:31.029
"I have something else to show you," said the priest.

57
00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:32.201
"Follow me."

58
00:03:32.202 --> 00:03:36.813
At the bottom of the stairs, behind a closet door, he showed her a basket.

59
00:03:36.814 --> 00:03:39.174
Heidi bent down and said with delight,

60
00:03:39.175 --> 00:03:42.365
"Oh, look at the sweet little kittens!"

61
00:03:42.366 --> 00:03:45.045
"Would you like to have them?" asked the priest.

62
00:03:45.046 --> 00:03:49.095
Heidi could hardly contain her joy.
